'''Jetpack Cat''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked when beating the [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] [[Reign of the Tyrant]] appearing on the '''3rd''', '''4th''', '''17th''' and '''18th''' days of every month. It was added in [[Version 12.3 Update|Version 12.3]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 708
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Jetpack Cat
|name2 = Kinjirou Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kinjirou Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is best used as a 'secondary' meatshield, a specialist that has a higher-than-average cost/recharge time in return for superior resilience against specific targets. In this case, Jetpack Cat proves to be a great meatshield against Alien enemies, and decent against Dark. Assuming all Void Fruit and Enigma Fruit Treasures are maxed, each Jetpack Cat has an impressive ''76K'' health at Level 30.

When compared to [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], Jetpack Cat gets a major win in the health category, over double what Catellite reaches at Level 30 at less than double the cost. While Catellite has the advantage of bonus levels and higher damage, Jetpack Cat has Area Attacks to deal with swarms of weak peons better and can be boosted itself to still compete health-wise. On top of being more expensive, Jetpack Cat also lacks the important [[Immune to Warp]] ability that Catellite has, so it does not fully supersede Catellite.

Against Dark enemies, Jetpack Cat fares worse but is still a decent option. Its primary competition is [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]], [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Nono]], and [[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Li'l Gau]], but Jetpack Cat still holds up. Against Gas Mask, Jetpack Cat has better health, damage and recharge, as well as lower range than [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]], making it the preferred option against non-[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemies. Both Nono and Li'l Gau have more range, with Nono losing out in health, although they do not suffer from long recharge timers as much as Jetpack and therefore need no assistance from Cat Combos like [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]], which can take up valuable slots. Furthermore, Nono and Li'l Gau do have notable abilities that Jetpack lacks (Immune to Curse + 50% Survive/Immune to Knockback) Still, Jetpack Cat will be the best option in most scenarios if the player lacks any of the three, as Gas Mask does have a somewhat long shopping list of Evolution Materials while Nono and Li'l Gau are Collab exclusive.

Finally, Colossus Slayer is a true game-changer for this unit. The only other Colossus meatshield that exists is [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]], so Jetpack Cat gains an immediate niche from it. Against Colossus threats not within its targeted traits, it has 22k HP which is higher than Manic Eraser so it doesn't get immediately outclassed. Against its Targeted Traits, however, Jetpack's stats are substantially better and reaches slightly more than '''109K''' HP against them. This, combined with its Immunity to Slow, naturally makes it a staple versus [[Super Hyppoh]] (who is supported by nasty Dark threats) and [[Le'Grim]], not to mention those yet to come. Jetpack Cat's damage also isn't too shabby at 1,876 DPS, so it can do decent damage against Colossus that will rack up over time. While Le'Grim might not be the worst opponent, the same cannot be said for Super Hyppoh's [[Horrorpotamus/Cosmic Juggernaut Lv.1~20|stages]], so its abilities are certainly a welcoming addition.

Overall, Jetpack Cat is an excellent unit that serves as a great reward for taking down one of the hardest advent bosses.

